{"baseRefName":"docs/kanna-walks","baseRefOid":"ba1b62c18b11a345e11d07baaad486261917c6e3","body":"## What changed\n\nThe largest slice (stack 4/5; base: PR 3 branch): home polish, `/support`, a real type scale, calmer docs chrome, colour practice and reduced-motion fixes.\n\n**Home** — mascot moves from above the h1 (it pushed the headline a third of the way down) to the terminal's top edge; the three equal cards become a scroll-driven timeline Kanna walks along; the hero terminal types `/search Dune` once (stops on first touch, never autoplays under reduced motion, fixed height so the hero stops jumping); start cards get icons; a support strip precedes the final CTA.\n\n**/support** — what sponsorship pays for, an honest empty sponsor wall (committed list, never a live fetch), free ways to help; `.github/FUNDING.yml` points at it. *The wording of the funding claims is a draft for the maintainer to confirm.*\n\n**Docs chrome** — the sidebar repeated eight site links above its own tree; only Releases and Analytics (not in the tree) stay, the rest live in the top bar and footer. The 8-fact beta callout (seven pages) is three labelled lines; duplicate banner on getting-started removed.\n\n**Type scale** — four weight names, 700/900 retired, 12px floor; the display serif is h1/h2 only (Cormorant's hairlines fail at 12–18px). The global heading rule moves into the base layer so `font-sans` on a small h2 actually wins.\n\n**Colour practice** — primary buttons use dark ink on rose (white measured 3.6:1, and 2.1:1 on hover); selected tab = accent text on accent fill; `border-input` → the 3:1 control edge; code comments 3.7:1 → 6.2:1; raw hex → tokens; oklab gradients.\n\n**Motion (from an animation review)** — palette selection no longer animates/shifts layout on arrow keys; dead animations removed (referenced keyframes that never existed); `MotionConfig reducedMotion=\"user\"` (the stylesheet rule never reached Motion's JS animations); non-link cards no longer lift; hover lifts gated; 16px terminal input (iOS zoom).\n\n## Verification evidence\n\nTested commit: this branch head. `rm -rf .next && bun run typecheck && bun run lint && bun run fmt:check && bun run test` in `apps/docs` → clean / 0 errors / clean / **359 pass, 0 fail**. `generated-metadata.json` regenerated for the getting-started edit (pre-push freshness check passes).\n\n- Rendered-pair scan in headless Chrome before/after (type combos, text < 12px, contrast on the real background): code-comment failures and the 9px meta failures are gone; weights are 400/500/600 (+ display 300/400).\n- Stress at 320px: no horizontal overflow on home, support, docs. Real-browser pass (Claude in Chrome) of home/support/analytics at desktop and 390px.\n- New tests: `palette` (muted ≥ 4.5:1, control edge ≥ 3:1, `border-input` wiring, comment override, caption floor, no 700/900), `support` (FUNDING.yml ↔ SPONSOR_URL, empty vs populated wall, entry points), `render` (sidebar carries only Releases and Analytics).\n- Not exercised: a real-touch device; Lighthouse performance is unchanged by this PR (see the follow-up PR).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Changeset: N/A (docs-only)\n- [x] `bun run guard`: N/A\n- [x] fmt / lint / test / typecheck pass locally (per package)\n- [ ] `bun run build` — run once on the top of the stack (PR 5), passes\n- [x] Live provider or Discord smokes skipped intentionally (docs only)\n","files":[{"path":".github/FUNDING.yml","additions":1,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/app/(home)/home-page-interactive.tsx","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/app/(home)/home-page-shell.tsx","additions":45,"deletions":48,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/app/global-error.tsx","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/app/global.css","additions":27,"deletions":15,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/docs/app/layout.tsx","additions":4,"deletions":10,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"apps/d